#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# weierstrass_half_period_w1

#% text
# `weierstrass_half_period_w1([g2, g3])` gives the half-period `omega1` of the Weierstrass functions of invariants `g2`, `g3`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The half-periods are the reduced basis of the period lattice: `tau = omega3/omega1` lies in the fundamental domain (`|Re tau| <= 1/2`, `|tau| >= 1`) and `omega1` has a positive real part; for real invariants with `g3 < 0` they are `-im` times those of `[g2, -g3]` (DLMF 23.10.18).

#% item
# `omega2 = -omega1 - omega3`; `weierstrass_p(u + 2 omega_k, [g2, g3]) = weierstrass_p(u, [g2, g3])`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
weierstrass_half_period_w1([11.0, 7.0])
#% output
#= 0.9270373386506859

#% cell
n(weierstrass_half_period_w1([1, 2]), 25)
#% output
#= 1.3083647626370968653240501853

#% cell
weierstrass_half_period_w1([0.5 + im, 1.0])
#% output
#= 0.6543470042388131 + 1.3134409876370876im

#% cell
weierstrass_half_period_w1([1, 0])
#% output
#= gamma(1/4)^2/(4*pi^(1/2))

#% cell
w = weierstrass_half_period_w1([1.0, 2.0]); weierstrass_p(0.3 + 2*w, [1, 2]) - weierstrass_p(0.3, [1, 2])
#% output
#= 8.881784197001252e-15

